<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shahverdi Khan (Khorshidi atabeg)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1597">1597</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shahverdi Khan was the last atabeg of the Khorshidi dynasty, which ruled Lesser Luristan in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/falak-ol-aflak">Falak-ol-Aflak</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorramabad">Khorramabad</a>. After he rebelled against the Safavid shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Abbas I</a>, he was captured and executed in 1597, and Luristan was given to Safavid-appointed governors.</p></div>
